% Stage 2. The three iteration shapes of docs/SQL-TRANSLATION.md §7, decided by
% what the first argument is after stage 1 — never by what it might evaluate to.

### name: agg.static.all
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((1, 2, 3), _ > 0)
--- expect
(((1 > 0) AND (2 > 0)) AND (3 > 0))
===
### name: agg.static.any
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ANY((1, 2), _ > 1)
--- expect
((1 > 1) OR (2 > 1))
===
### name: agg.static.sum
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
SUM((1, 2, 3), _ * 2)
--- expect
(((1 * 2) + (2 * 2)) + (3 * 2))
===
### name: agg.static.one-element-needs-no-fold
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((5), _ > 0)
--- expect
(5 > 0)
===
### name: agg.static.named-binder
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((1, 2), N, N > 0)
--- expect
((1 > 0) AND (2 > 0))
===
### name: agg.static.key-binding
--- note
_K is the element's key. On a static list those are "1", "2", … exactly as `,`
builds them.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((7, 8), _K $!= "")
--- expect
((CAST('1' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin <> CAST('' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin) AND (CAST('2' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin <> CAST('' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin))
===
### name: agg.static.join
--- note
Pairwise through the dialect's own concatenation, because `&` is what SEL's
JOIN is. A variadic concat would need a lexical key spelled two ways for one
function.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
JOIN((1, 2, 3), "-")
--- expect
CONCAT(CONCAT(CONCAT(CONCAT(1, '-'), 2), '-'), 3)
===
### name: agg.static.count-folds-to-a-literal
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
COUNT((1, 2, 3))
--- expect
3
===
### name: agg.nested.static
--- note
The outer ALL folds two composite fragments, so the parentheses nest. A fold
combines the operands it is handed, not the ones inside them.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
R[1] = (1, 2); R[2] = (3, 4); ALL(R, ROW, ALL(ROW, _ > 0))
--- expect
(((1 > 0) AND (2 > 0)) AND ((3 > 0) AND (4 > 0)))
===
### name: agg.scalar.is-a-one-element-list
--- note
spec §7.3: a value with no children behaves as a one-element list containing
itself. This is the rule, not a convenience for the translator.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"TOTAL": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "total", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL(TOTAL, _ > 0)
--- expect
(`o`.`total` > 0)
===
### name: agg.columns.unroll
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}, {"table": "x", "column": "b", "type": "NUM"}, {"table": "x", "column": "c", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
ALL(V, C, C > 0)
--- expect
(((`x`.`a` > 0) AND (`x`.`b` > 0)) AND (`x`.`c` > 0))
===
### name: agg.columns.two-level-spelling
--- note
The inner ALL sees one column, and the scalar rule above turns it into a
one-element list. So the brief's ALL(values, val, ALL(row, …)) shape works
without a special case anywhere.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}, {"table": "x", "column": "b", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
ALL(V, C, ALL(C, _ > 0))
--- expect
((`x`.`a` > 0) AND (`x`.`b` > 0))
===
### name: agg.columns.key-is-the-ordinal
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
ALL(V, C, _K $== "1")
--- expect
(CAST('1' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = CAST('1' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)
===
### name: agg.columns.count-folds-to-a-literal
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"table": "x", "column": "a"}, {"table": "x", "column": "b"}]}}
--- source
COUNT(V)
--- expect
2
===
### name: agg.relation.all
--- note
IS NOT TRUE rather than NOT (…): with a NULL body, NOT (body) is NULL, the
WHERE rejects the row, and NOT EXISTS reports that every row satisfied it —
silently the wrong answer for the case a validation rule exists to catch.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}, "SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
ALL(ITEMS, I, I["qty"] > 0)
--- expect
NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id` AND ((`oi`.`qty` > 0)) IS NOT TRUE)
===
### name: agg.relation.any
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ANY(ITEMS, I, I["qty"] > 100)
--- expect
EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id` AND ((`oi`.`qty` > 100)) IS TRUE)
===
### name: agg.relation.sum
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}, "PRICE": {"table": "oi", "column": "price", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
SUM(ITEMS, _["QTY"] * _["PRICE"])
--- expect
(SELECT COALESCE(SUM((`oi`.`qty` * `oi`.`price`)), 0) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`)
===
### name: agg.relation.count
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
COUNT(ITEMS) == 0
--- expect
((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`) = 0)
===
### name: agg.relation.uncorrelated
--- note
{corr} fills with the dialect's TRUE when the binding names no correlation. A
subquery over the whole table is legal and occasionally what you want.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ALL_ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
COUNT(ALL_ITEMS)
--- expect
(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE TRUE)
===
### name: agg.relation.from-may-carry-a-query
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "relation", "from": {"raw": "(SELECT a, b FROM x)"}, "alias": "v", "fields": {"A": {"table": "v", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ALL(V, _["A"] > 0)
--- expect
NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM (SELECT a, b FROM x) `v` WHERE TRUE AND ((`v`.`a` > 0)) IS NOT TRUE)
===
### name: agg.relation.in
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"SKU": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}, "ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
SKU IN ITEMS
--- expect
(CAST(`o`.`sku` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin IN (SELECT CAST(`oi`.`sku` AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`))
===
### name: agg.relation.nested
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}, "LINES": {"kind": "relation", "from": "lines", "alias": "l", "correlate": {"raw": "`l`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "l", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ALL(ORDERS, O, ALL(LINES, L, L["qty"] > 0))
--- expect
NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `orders` `o` WHERE TRUE AND (NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `lines` `l` WHERE `l`.`order_id` = `o`.`id` AND ((`l`.`qty` > 0)) IS NOT TRUE)) IS NOT TRUE)
===
### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-all
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL(FILTER((1, 2, 3), _ > 1), _ > 2)
--- expect
((((NOT (1 > 1)) OR (1 > 2)) AND ((NOT (2 > 1)) OR (2 > 2))) AND ((NOT (3 > 1)) OR (3 > 2)))
===
### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-any
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ANY(FILTER((1, 2), _ > 1), _ > 0)
--- expect
(((1 > 1) AND (1 > 0)) OR ((2 > 1) AND (2 > 0)))
===
### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-count
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
COUNT(FILTER(ITEMS, _["QTY"] <= 0)) > 0
--- expect
((SELECT COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN (`oi`.`qty` <= 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), 0) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`) > 0)
===
### name: agg.filter.different-binder-names
--- note
Absorption binds both names to the same element rather than substituting one
for the other. That is why it is three lines and cannot get a substitution
wrong.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL(FILTER((1, 2), A, A > 1), B, B > 2)
--- expect
(((NOT (1 > 1)) OR (1 > 2)) AND ((NOT (2 > 1)) OR (2 > 2)))
===
### name: agg.filter.nested-filters-conjoin
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL(FILTER(FILTER((1, 2), _ > 0), _ > 1), _ > 2)
--- expect
(((NOT (1 > 1)) OR ((NOT (1 > 0)) OR (1 > 2))) AND ((NOT (2 > 1)) OR ((NOT (2 > 0)) OR (2 > 2))))
===
### name: agg.value.binding-as-a-list
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"L": {"kind": "value", "value": {"1": "a", "2": "b"}}}
--- source
ALL(L, _ $!= "")
--- expect
((CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin <> CAST('' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin) AND (CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin <> CAST('' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_bin))
===
### name: agg.empty.all-is-true
--- note
spec §7.3: an empty list makes ALL true and ANY false. A NONE with no children
is genuinely empty — it is what FILTER returns when nothing matched.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"E": {"kind": "value", "value": []}}
--- source
ALL(E, _ > 0)
--- expect
TRUE
===
### name: agg.empty.any-is-false
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"E": {"kind": "value", "value": []}}
--- source
ANY(E, _ > 0)
--- expect
FALSE
===
### name: agg.empty.sum-is-zero
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"E": {"kind": "value", "value": []}}
--- source
SUM(E, _ * 2)
--- expect
0
===
### name: agg.has.static-is-decided-at-translation-time
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
HAS((1, 2), "2")
--- expect
TRUE
===
### name: agg.has.relation-field
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
HAS(ITEMS, "price")
--- expect
FALSE
===
### name: agg.refuse.k-on-a-relation
--- note
A row has no portable key. Inventing one — ROW_NUMBER(), the primary key —
would be a guess about the schema this layer never makes.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ALL(ITEMS, _K $!= "")
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:12
===
### name: agg.refuse.relation-indexed-by-position
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
ITEMS[1]
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:6
===
### name: agg.refuse.bare-row-without-a-scalar
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ALL(ITEMS, I, I > 0)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:15
===
### name: agg.refuse.non-bool-body
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((1, 2), _ + 1)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:15
===
### name: agg.refuse.non-num-body-for-sum
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
SUM((1, 2), _ > 0)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:15
===
### name: agg.refuse.map-in-a-value-position
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
MAP((1, 2), _ * 2)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: agg.refuse.join-over-a-relation
--- note
The reason comes from the map: GROUP_CONCAT does not specify an order without
an ORDER BY, and SEL's JOIN concatenates in insertion order.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
JOIN(ITEMS, ", ")
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===
### name: agg.refuse.binder-must-be-a-name
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((1, 2), 5, _ > 0)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:13
### name: agg.contract.over-credit-limit
--- note
§7.8's worked contract, as cases rather than as prose. The block in the document
quotes these; php/bin/sqldoc checks the quotation.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}, "PRICE": {"table": "oi", "column": "price", "type": "NUM"}, "SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}, "CREDIT_LIMIT": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "credit_limit", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
SUM(ITEMS, _["QTY"] * _["PRICE"]) > CREDIT_LIMIT
--- expect
((SELECT COALESCE(SUM((`oi`.`qty` * `oi`.`price`)), 0) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`) > `o`.`credit_limit`)
===
### name: agg.contract.all-skus-well-formed
--- note
The (?s) prefix is folded into the pattern text, not concatenated at run time.
The document claimed REGEXP CONCAT('(?s)', …) for two milestones, which is what
this quotation now stops.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}, "PRICE": {"table": "oi", "column": "price", "type": "NUM"}, "SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}, "CREDIT_LIMIT": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "credit_limit", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL(ITEMS, RMATCH('^[A-Z]{2}-\d{4}$', _["SKU"]))
--- expect
NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id` AND ((`oi`.`sku` COLLATE utf8mb4_bin REGEXP '(?s)^[A-Z]{2}-[0-9]{4}$')) IS NOT TRUE)
===
### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-count-bare
--- note
§7.5's example: COUNT over an absorbed FILTER with a named binder, without the
comparison agg.filter.absorbed-into-count wraps it in.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "correlate": {"raw": "`oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`"}, "scalar": "SKU", "fields": {"QTY": {"table": "oi", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}, "PRICE": {"table": "oi", "column": "price", "type": "NUM"}, "SKU": {"table": "oi", "column": "sku", "type": "TEXT"}}}, "CREDIT_LIMIT": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "credit_limit", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
COUNT(FILTER(ITEMS, I, I["qty"] <= 0))
--- expect
(SELECT COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN (`oi`.`qty` <= 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), 0) FROM `order_items` `oi` WHERE `oi`.`order_id` = `o`.`id`)
===
